  "title": "Erdős Problem #696",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $h(n)$ be the largest $\\ell$ such that there is a sequence of primes $p_1<\\cdots < p_\\ell$ all dividing $n$ with $p_{i+1}\\equiv 1\\pmod{p_i}$. Let $H(n)$ be the largest $u$ such that there is a sequence of integers $d_1<\\cdots < d_u$ all dividing $n$ with $d_{i+1}\\equiv 1\\pmod{d_i}$.\nEstimate $h(n)$ and $H(n)$. Is it true that $H(n)/h(n)\\to \\infty$ for almost all $n$?",
